## Summary

I found and fixed the bug in src/parse.py:4. The issue was a classic off-by-one error where the function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). 

This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError since there's no index 1

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`. All tests now pass.
